<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Daik</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Daik is a town on Lingga Island in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riau-archipelago">Riau Islands</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>. From the late 18th century it was the seat of the sultans of Johor-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riau">Riau</a> and later of the Riau-Lingga Sultanate, while the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bugis">Bugis</a> viceroys governed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penyengat">Penyengat</a>. Ruins of the royal palace and an old mosque survive.</p></div>
